// A file-scope CONST matrix folds into the ucode and gets NO container
// record (t_4b54f26b A3).
//
// evaluateConstInitializerTyped capped a constructor at four arguments, so a
// 3x3 built from nine scalars refused with "file-scope const 'M' has an
// initialiser this compiler cannot evaluate".  Eight reference-SDK rows were
// that one shape, all of them including a single shared logluv.cg.
//
// Measured on the reference: the container is TWO records - the entry
// parameter and the output - and M appears nowhere.  The record COUNT is the
// assertion that matters: if a future change starts emitting parent/row
// records for a const matrix it will still produce correct values and the
// count is the only thing that catches it.
//
// The rows are read through M[i] rather than mul(M, v) ON PURPOSE: mul with a
// matrix operand is a separate, still-open refusal in the fragment profile
// (matvecmul, t_741ac502; vecmatmul, t_f16cb660), and a fixture that tripped
// over those would be testing somebody else's gap instead of this one.
// ASYMMETRIC values, so a transposed or mis-ordered fold cannot pass.
const static float3x3 M = float3x3
	(
	   0.25, 0.5, 0.75,
	   1.5, 2.5, 3.5,
	   -1.0, -2.0, -4.0
	);

float4 main(float2 uv : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR
{
	return float4(M[0] * uv.x + M[1] * uv.y + M[2], 1.0);
}
